Erm, 'anachronistic' means something from the "wrong time" (someone in
a  historical film playing in old roman times wearing a wristwatch,
say). The crossbow is listed as having been known in China since ~1000
BC. And it stayed in use well into the time kung-fu became popular. So
not much leeway for anachronism there, really.

Even more importantly, a german site about the Shaolin monastery
mentions the crossbow among the traditional weapons the monks there
train with regularly (also including whips and various sorts of sword,
as well as the nunchaku).

